# Sanitized Wazuh Manager Configuration Example

This is a simplified documentation example based on the lab configuration. It is not a copy of the complete production configuration.

```xml
<ossec_config>

  <!-- Enable JSON event archiving -->
  <global>
    <logall_json>yes</logall_json>
    <logall>no</logall>
  </global>

  <!-- Internal Indexer connection example -->
  <indexer>
    <enabled>yes</enabled>
    <hosts>
      <host>https://127.0.0.1:9200</host>
    </hosts>
  </indexer>

</ossec_config>
```

## Configuration notes

- `logall_json` enables JSON archiving of collected events.
- `logall` remains disabled.
- The Indexer address uses the local server interface.
- The archive file is stored at `/var/ossec/logs/archives/archives.json`.

**Important:** This is a simplified illustrative example. Do not replace your actual `/var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf` with this file. Your real Manager configuration contains additional required sections.

**Security:** Never publish credentials, private keys, certificates, or raw event archives.